;; slog-lint: a static analysis of Slog programs, written in Slog.
;;
;; compiler/reify.rkt reads a program with the compiler's own parser and
;; writes it as facts over schema.slog: its declarations, rules, clauses
;; and terms, each at its line and column.  The analysis reads those facts
;; and derives `finding` rows -- (finding Severity File Line Col Code
;; Message) -- along with the relations Studio shows beside the program
;; (writer, reader, dep, recursive, inhabited, never_fires, demand_calls).
;;
;; It comes in three tiers, each including the one before, so a runner can
;; show the quick findings first:
;;   lint-local.slog   each rule on its own: variables, arity, shapes
;;   lint-graph.slog   the dependency graph: recursion, negation, dead rules
;;   lint-deep.slog    demands and constructors across the program
;;
;; This file is the whole analysis over one program's facts:
;;
;;   racket compiler/reify.rkt PROGRAM.slog > analysis/facts.slog
;;   racket compiler/run.rkt analysis/slog-lint.slog
;;
;; Studio runs the tiers on every edit (studio/src/lint.rs), reading the
;; facts from a database rather than compiling them; "Edit the analysis"
;; opens this directory as a project, with facts.slog the program you came
;; from, so the analysis can be run, debugged and edited like any program.
;; analysis/test.rkt holds it to its tests.

include "lint-deep.slog"
include "facts.slog"
